<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="chapter-stacked-polynomials">
  <title>Adding and Subtracting Polynomials</title>
  <introduction>
    <p><em>AF3(a)(i)–(ii).</em> Align like terms vertically. The layout is the same idea as column addition with numbers: each power of <m>x</m> has its own column. There are no brackets in this display arrangement.</p>
    <p><em>Subtracting?</em> Subtract the <em>entire</em> lower row. Change the sign of every lower term before collecting like terms, not merely the first term. A horizontal line separates the question from the answer.</p>
    <p>In each block of six, odd-numbered exercises have worked solutions; even-numbered exercises provide an answer for checking.</p>
  </introduction>
  <section xml:id="stacked-polynomials-linear">
    <title>Linear expressions: align the variable columns</title>
    <example xml:id="stacked-linear-example">
      <title>Subtract the entire lower row</title>
      <statement>
        <me>\begin{array}{rrrr}&amp;5x&amp;-2y&amp;+3\\-&amp;2x&amp;+4y&amp;-5\\\hline\end{array}</me>
      </statement>
      <solution>
        <me>(5x-2x)+(-2y-4y)+(3+5)=3x-6y+8.</me>
        <p>Although the lower row contains <m>+4y-5</m>, subtraction makes its contributions <m>-4y+5</m>.</p>
      </solution>
    </example>
  </section>
  <section xml:id="stacked-polynomials-quadratic">
    <title>Quadratic expressions: six mixed questions</title>
    <p>Work down each column. Do the additions and subtractions directly; you do not need a special computer algebra macro to write these questions.</p>
    <exercise xml:id="stacked-poly-1"><statement><p>Add.</p><me>\begin{array}{rrrr}&amp;3x^2&amp;+2x&amp;-5\\+&amp;4x^2&amp;-7x&amp;+3\\\hline\end{array}</me></statement><solution><p><m>7x^2-5x-2</m>. Coefficients by column: <m>3+4=7</m>, <m>2-7=-5</m>, <m>-5+3=-2</m>.</p></solution></exercise>
    <exercise xml:id="stacked-poly-2"><statement><p>Subtract.</p><me>\begin{array}{rrrr}&amp;5x^2&amp;-3x&amp;+8\\-&amp;2x^2&amp;+x&amp;-4\\\hline\end{array}</me></statement><answer><p><m>3x^2-4x+12</m>.</p></answer></exercise>
    <exercise xml:id="stacked-poly-3"><statement><p>Add.</p><me>\begin{array}{rrrr}&amp;2x^2&amp;+3x&amp;-6\\+&amp;-x^2&amp;+5x&amp;+2\\\hline\end{array}</me></statement><solution><p><m>x^2+8x-4</m>. The lower leading term is already negative: <m>2x^2+(-x^2)=x^2</m>.</p></solution></exercise>
    <exercise xml:id="stacked-poly-4"><statement><p>Subtract.</p><me>\begin{array}{rrrr}&amp;4x^2&amp;+x&amp;-7\\-&amp;x^2&amp;-3x&amp;+6\\\hline\end{array}</me></statement><answer><p><m>3x^2+4x-13</m>.</p></answer></exercise>
    <exercise xml:id="stacked-poly-5"><statement><p>Add.</p><me>\begin{array}{rrrr}&amp;x^2&amp;-4x&amp;+9\\+&amp;2x^2&amp;+6x&amp;-1\\\hline\end{array}</me></statement><solution><p><m>3x^2+2x+8</m>. Combine corresponding coefficients only: <m>1+2</m>, <m>-4+6</m>, <m>9-1</m>.</p></solution></exercise>
    <exercise xml:id="stacked-poly-6"><statement><p>Subtract.</p><me>\begin{array}{rrrr}&amp;3x^2&amp;-2x&amp;+1\\-&amp;-2x^2&amp;+5x&amp;-4\\\hline\end{array}</me></statement><answer><p><m>5x^2-7x+5</m>.</p></answer></exercise>
    <p>Notice the inverse habit: after completing an addition or subtraction, recover the missing original polynomial to check your result.</p>
  </section>
</chapter>
